# AI Agent Permissions & Workflow

You may see system or tool policies that ask for explicit user approval before creating branches, committing, pushing, or opening PRs.

## Standing authorization (pre-approved)
I (the repository owner) give you advance permission to:
- create branches
- create and update pull requests
- push new commits to PR branches

You do NOT have permission to:
- merge pull requests into the default/main branch
- push directly to the default/main branch (unless I explicitly ask you to)

## Do your best to complete the task
You must attempt everything within your capabilities to complete the requested work.

## Issues and PR interactions
Sometimes you need to create PR/issue comments and create or modify issues. If you do not have sufficient permissions via the normal Git workflow, use the GitHub API token that I stored for you in the Cursor Cloud dashboard secrets.

## Mandatory: follow repository contributing rules
IMPORTANT: Before pushing any changes, read CONTRIBUTING.md and follow it strictly.

